\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \fi0 The reaction pathways, including five individual steps (R1-R5) as shown in Figure 1b, were established under integral operating conditions. When using guaiacol as feed, under differential operating conditions (guaiacol conversion less than 6-8%), catechol is the only product generated, i.e. only step R1 prevails while steps R3 and R4 are negligible. When catechol is used as feed, also under differential conditions, both phenol and cyclopentanone (corresponding to steps R2 and R5) exist in the liquid products. These experimental observations imply that when feeding guaiacol under differential operating conditions, R1 is faster than R3 and R4, and phenol and cyclopentanone are not produced owing to low concentration of catechol. Therefore, kinetic parameters for steps R1, R2 and R5 could be obtained by running differential reactions. Using kinetic parameters of R1, R2 and R5, those for R3 and R4 could be further regressed by running integral reactions.\par
\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \fi0 When differential operating conditions apply, reaction rates are obtained by Eq. ({\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMEq3 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{3}}}). {\par
