}\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \fi0 Using H{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 2})}}{\fldrslt }}
} as reductant, Runnebaum et al. 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Runnebaum2012 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{31}{2012}{{Runnebaum et\~al.}}{{Runnebaum, Nimmanwudipong, Block, and Gates}}}}}
] also reported 1st order kinetics for step R1 over Pt/Al{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ {\\s\\do5({\fs16 2})}}}{\fldrslt }}
}O{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ {\\s\\do5({\fs16 3})}}}{\fldrslt }}
} catalyst, while our prior work 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Gao2015 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{23}{2015}{{Gao et\~al.}}{{Gao, Xiao, and Varma}}}}}
] fitted a 2nd order for the same step. The difference between the present work and our prior work may be due to different reductants (H{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 2})}}{\fldrslt }}
} or CH{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 4})}}{\fldrslt }}
}). For steps R2 and R5, both the present work and our prior work demonstrate 1st order kinetics. The reaction rate constant values, however, are smaller when CH{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 4})}}{\fldrslt }}
} is used as reductant, indicating a higher activation energy for CH{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 4})}}{\fldrslt }}
}.\par
\pard\plain\s4\ql\sb240\sa120\keepn\f0\b\fs32\sl240\slmult1 \sb120 \fi0 6.5  Integral Reactions of Steps R3 and R4\par
\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \sb60 \fi0 As shown above, under differential operating conditions, step R1 is decomposed from the reaction network (Figure 1) when feeding guaiacol over the catalyst. Similarly, steps R2 and R5 are decomposed under differential operating conditions when feeding catechol. To obtain insight into steps R3 and R4, integral operating conditions were used while feeding guaiacol by packing more catalyst, producing distinct amounts of phenol and cyclopentanone. These, obviously, introduce not only steps R3 and R4, but also steps R1, R2 and R5. Thus Eqs. ({\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMEq4 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{4}}} -\~{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMEq7 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{7}}}) can be re-written as Eqs. ({\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMEq22 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{13}}} -\~{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMEq25 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{16}}}), where {{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ {\i k}\\s\\do5({\fs16 {\i i}})}}{\fldrslt }}
} and {{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ {\i n}\\s\\do5({\fs16 {\i i}})}}{\fldrslt }}
} are reaction rate constants and orders for steps {{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ {\i R}\\s\\do5({\fs16 {\i i}})}}{\fldrslt }}
}.\par
